            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A clamping device (400) for a shaft of a catheter includes a first member (402) rotatably coupled to a second member (401). The first member (402) has an annular element (426) defining a central lumen (408), the outer surface of the annular element (426) having a non-circular cross-sectional profile, and the second member (401) defines a bore into which the annular element (426) extends, the bore having a non-circular cross-sectional profile. The device (400) can move between a release state wherein the central lumen (408) has a first diameter, and a clamped state wherein the central lumen (408) has a second diameter less than the first diameter.</p>
            </abstract>
